---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Panel from '../../components/Panel.astro';
import icon from '../../assets/icon.png';
// Source of truth: cli/src/main.rs and engine/src/ipc.rs. Update this page when they change.
---

<Base title="The dl command | Rays by a6n" description="Start and list Rays downloads from Terminal with the dl command.">
	<div class="page">
		<main id="main" class="column">
			<header class="mark">
				<a href="/" class="home">
					<Image src={icon} alt="" width={28} height={28} />
					<span>Rays</span>
				</a>
				<span class="by">by <a href="https://a6n.ai">a6n</a></span>
			</header>

			<article class="doc">
				<h1>The <code>dl</code> command</h1>
				<p class="lead">One command for Rays: download links, sort folders, and connect AI assistants over MCP.</p>

				<h2>Install</h2>
				<p>The Homebrew install puts <code>dl</code> on your PATH:</p>
				<pre><code>brew install --cask a6n-ai/tap/rays</code></pre>
				<p>
					If you installed from the DMG, the command is inside the app. Link it once:
				</p>
				<pre><code>ln -s /Applications/Rays.app/Contents/MacOS/dl /opt/homebrew/bin/dl</code></pre>

				<h2>Download files</h2>
				<pre><code>dl URL...</code></pre>
				<p>Give one or more links. Each one is added to Rays and starts when a slot is free.</p>
				<pre><code>dl https://example.com/file.zip https://example.com/talk.mp4</code></pre>
				<p>For each link, <code>dl</code> prints one line:</p>
				<pre><code>added 12 https://example.com/file.zip
rejected ftp://example.com/x: only http and https URLs</code></pre>
				<p>Only <code>http</code> and <code>https</code> links are accepted.</p>

				<h2>List downloads</h2>
				<pre><code>dl list</code></pre>
				<p>One line per download: id, state, bytes done / total, file name. Fields are separated by tabs (shown as spaces here).</p>
				<pre><code>12  running  52428800/104857600  file.zip
11  done     7340032/7340032     report.pdf</code></pre>
				<p>
					The state is one of <code>queued</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>paused</code>,{' '}
					<code>retrying</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>failed</code>. The total shows <code>?</code> when the
					server does not say how big the file is.
				</p>

				<h2>Sort a folder</h2>
				<pre><code>dl sort [FOLDER] [--all] [--dry-run] [--projects]</code></pre>
				<p>
					Moves files into category folders such as Work, Images, Installers and Archives, inside FOLDER. Without a
					folder it sorts <code>~/Downloads</code>; <code>.</code> is the current folder.
				</p>
				<table>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>--dry-run</code></td><td>Print what would move and change nothing.</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>--all</code></td><td>Also sort files that were there before the first run.</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>--projects</code></td><td>Move code-project folders whole into Code/Projects.</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p>Files changed in the last 10 seconds are skipped, so nothing moves while it is still being written.</p>
				<pre><code>dl sort ~/Desktop --dry-run
[dry] setup.dmg -&gt; ~/Desktop/Installers/Apps/Setup.dmg (Installers/Apps rule)</code></pre>

				<h2>Watch a folder</h2>
				<pre><code>dl watch ~/Downloads
dl unwatch ~/Downloads</code></pre>
				<p>Rays sorts the folder by itself whenever a new file lands in it, even when the app is closed.</p>

				<h2>Sorter status and settings</h2>
				<pre><code>dl status
dl status --json</code></pre>
				<p>Shows the wait time, whether renaming is on, the folders Rays sorts, and the last moves.</p>
				<pre><code>dl config set-wait 30
dl config set-rename off
dl config set-dest ~/Downloads Work ~/Documents/Work
dl config clear-dest ~/Downloads Work</code></pre>
				<p>
					<code>set-wait</code> is in seconds. <code>set-dest</code> sends one category somewhere else instead of a
					folder inside the sorted folder.
				</p>

				<h2>AI assistants (MCP)</h2>
				<pre><code>dl mcp</code></pre>
				<p>
					Runs a Model Context Protocol server on stdin and stdout, so assistants like Claude can use Rays. Add it
					to Claude Code:
				</p>
				<pre><code>claude mcp add rays -- dl mcp</code></pre>
				<p>Or to any MCP client config:</p>
				<pre><code>{'{"mcpServers": {"rays": {"command": "dl", "args": ["mcp"]}}}'}</code></pre>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>add_downloads</code></td><td>Download one or more http or https links.</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>list_downloads</code></td><td>Downloads with state, progress and file name.</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>sorter_status</code></td><td>Watched folders, categories, settings and recent moves.</td></tr>
						<tr>
							<td><code>sort_folder</code></td>
							<td>Sort a folder. A dry run unless the assistant sets <code>dry_run</code> to false.</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<h2>When Rays is not open</h2>
				<p>
					<code>dl</code> opens Rays for you and waits up to 5 seconds for it to start. Set
					<code>DL_NO_LAUNCH=1</code> to stop it opening the app.
				</p>

				<h2>Exit codes</h2>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th scope="col">Code</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>0</code></td><td>The command worked: every link was added, or the list, status or sort finished.</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>1</code></td><td>At least one link was rejected, or Rays returned an error.</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>2</code></td><td>Wrong usage, or Rays or the sorter could not be reached.</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<h2>Environment</h2>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th scope="col">Variable</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td><code>DL_NO_LAUNCH</code></td>
							<td>If set, <code>dl</code> does not open Rays when it is not running.</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td><code>DL_SORTER</code></td>
							<td>Path of the sorter to run, instead of the one inside Rays.app.</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td><code>DL_SOCKET</code></td>
							<td>
								Path of the socket to talk to, instead of
								<code>~/Library/Application Support/Rays/dl.sock</code>. Never opens the app.
							</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<h2>Scripts</h2>
				<p>Download every link in a file, one per line:</p>
				<pre><code>xargs dl &lt; links.txt</code></pre>
				<p>Stop a script when a link is rejected:</p>
				<pre><code>dl "$URL" || echo "Rays did not take $URL"</code></pre>
			</article>

			<footer class="foot">
				<a href="/">Rays home</a>
				<span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<a href="/releases/">Release notes</a>
				<a href="https://github.com/a6n-ai/rays">GitHub</a>
			</footer>
		</main>
		<Panel />
	</div>
</Base>

